[1m[38;5;231mWhich surface does the logging need to cover?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m Browser app.js only (Recommended)
     [38;5;246mLeveled logger plus a remote sink for the login form. The real debugging pain and the real PII risk both live here.
[39m  [38;5;246m2.[39m Node src/index.js only
     [38;5;246mStructured logs to stdout with an env-var level. Cheap and self-contained, but src/index.js has almost nothing to [39m
     [38;5;246mdebug.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Both, shared core
     [38;5;246mOne logger API, two transports. Consistent, but a runtime-neutral abstraction is heavy for two files this size.[39m
